AB  - The fugitive dust concentration measurement method and the system are presented based on light scattering when a single wavelength laser goes through fugitive dust. The system approximates the real particle size distribution by a bimodal normal distribution model and calculates fugitive dust concentration in an opening light-path real-timely. There are a wide dynamic range and a real-time response speed, so it's appropriate for the measurement of fugitive dust with a high concentration, a fast change and a wide range. The feasibility and reliability is proved by hydrosol experiments and smoke dust tests. Experimental results show that the system can cover a concentration measurement range of 0~400mg/m3 with a resolution of 0.05mg/m3, and finish a measurement in less than 1s. © 2016, Editorial Board of Optical Technique. All right reserved.
