AB  - Measuring the size and concentration of fine particulate matter in the air is of high importance for big cities with a population of more than 1 million people. Optical devices are used with the functions of determining the parameters and distribution of particles by size. The principle of operation of such devices is diffuse laser radiation. The article provides an analysis of the method for finding the above mentioned parameters based on the concept of Mie diffraction and the assumption that fine particles are of spherical shape. The scattering curves of laser radiation indicatrices on dust particles 2.5 and 10 μm in size were calculated, and the particle size allocation function was estimated under the condition of determining the intensity of diffuse light at more than 2 angles at which scattering occurs. The possibility of misinterpretation of the results of measurements by widely used portable measuring devices for the parameters of dust particles is shown.  © 2023 IEEE.
